# Wave W17-X (Route 209): bell pine — a quiet pine in still sage-greens, tiered and unhurried, its highlight lifted clear of the turf, on tower turf (ground baked in). Route 209’s own tree — split from Route 210’s paddock pine by crown temperature (sage quiet vs pasture warmth) and from Route 203’s dusted coal pine by register entire: no dust settles here, only petals.
